rsswitchd
=========

rsswitchd is a Raspberry Pi network daemon process for controlling remote
socket switches.

rsswitchd links against librsswitch [1] and uses function socket_send() of
librsswitch to switch a given socket either on or off.

Installation (Raspberry Pi)
===========================
 $ cd librsswitch/examples/network/
 $ make rpi     # or: make rpi3 on a 64-bit Raspberry Pi OS
 $ sudo make install

rsswitchd is installed to /usr/local/bin and enabled and started via
systemd by default. For a staged install (packaging, or checking the
result without root), use `make install DESTDIR=<dir>`: the binary
and unit file are placed under <dir> and the systemd steps are
skipped.

Installation (x86_64 host)
===========================
From examples/network:
 $ make x86_64
 $ make install DESTDIR=/tmp/rsswitchd-stage
 $ ls /tmp/rsswitchd-stage/usr/local/bin/rsswitchd /tmp/rsswitchd-stage/etc/systemd/system/rsswitchd.service

Usage
=======================
rsswitchd is listening on port 5000 for commands from
connected clients. It needs the following information
to switch a socket:

- dev: Vendor ID (check the wiki for the list of supported devices)
- group: Socket group
- socket: Socket within a socket group
- data: 1 = On, 0 = Off

See [2] for a detailed description.

Netcat
----------
echo -n "0300" | nc 192.168.2.19 5000

[1] https://github.com/graznik/librsswitch
[2] https://github.com/graznik/librsswitch/wiki#usage
